# Gate step 1924-dobj — darwin's unpacked debuginfo leaves loose .o files that
# cargo never collects; build.sh prunes every group no linked executable can
# read. The fixture proves an executable's own objects are kept, a library's
# loose objects are pruned, nothing else is touched, and a rerun prunes nothing.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf). Ported to Lua by 2106-scrt
# (scratch.* reaches the fixture's target dir; the regime pin is the .sh run).
STEP_DESC="Checking the darwin stale-object prune keeps what binaries read (1924-dobj)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/test-prune-darwin-stale-objects.lua"
STEP_ERROR="the darwin stale-object prune removed a linked executable's objects, kept a stale group, or touched a non-object file (1924-dobj) — see the FAIL lines above"
STEP_OK="Darwin stale-object prune fixture passed"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="tlatoanis-macbook-air 2026-10-29 darwin ok:prune-darwin-stale-objects:7"
# ORDER 2157-ginp: STEP_READS, the paths this step reads, RECORDED ONLY: never
# consulted by the class-selector skip (that is STEP_INPUTS, 2118-tnut). First
# cut: the step's own script plus every repo path it names literally.
STEP_READS="scripts/lua/prune-darwin-stale-objects.lua scripts/lua/test-prune-darwin-stale-objects.lua"
